<Layout
  title="Meta nuclear package - Hardware - Rycode"
  description="Meta's January 2026 nuclear deals with Vistra, TerraPower, and Oklo: up to 6.6 GW of new and existing clean energy by 2035."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Hardware · Power</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Meta nuclear package</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">On 9 January 2026 Meta announced deals with three nuclear companies, Vistra, TerraPower, and Oklo, that support up to 6.6 GW of new and existing clean energy by 2035 (<a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/01/meta-nuclear-energy-projects-power-american-ai-leadership/">Meta, 9 Jan 2026</a>). The power goes into the grids that serve Meta's data centers, including <a href="/ai/hardware/data-centers/prometheus/">Prometheus</a> in Ohio.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">The three deals</h2>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Partner</th><th scope="col">What it is</th><th scope="col">Size</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Vistra</td><td>20-year purchases from Perry and Davis-Besse (Ohio), plus uprates there and at Beaver Valley (Pennsylvania)</td><td>More than 2.1 GW bought; 433 MW of uprates</td><td>Uprates early 2030s</td></tr>
          <tr><td>TerraPower</td><td>Two new Natrium reactors, with rights to six more</td><td>690 MW for the first two; 2.8 GW for all eight, plus 1.2 GW of built-in storage</td><td>As early as 2032; the rest by 2035</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Oklo</td><td>New Aurora reactors in Pike County, Ohio</td><td>Up to 1.2 GW</td><td>As early as 2030</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>A GW is a billion watts and an MW a million. An uprate is an upgrade that lets an existing reactor make more power. Natrium is TerraPower's reactor design with built-in heat storage. PJM is the grid operator for much of the eastern US, including Ohio and Pennsylvania.</p>
    <p>Meta counts these with an earlier Constellation deal for a plant in Clinton, Illinois. The figures are Meta's own and are plans, not power delivered today.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/01/meta-nuclear-energy-projects-power-american-ai-leadership/">Meta, nuclear energy projects (9 Jan 2026)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
